{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1551608233,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0MTY0OTg4NTc=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3192","origin":"github"},"title":"Restructure source tree","message":"I believe we agree that the source tree is a bit out of sync with the internal (dependency) structure of the code. I would like to propose a restructuring as follows (lumping together stuff that is scattered across -core and the -revolution extension for now):\n\n- [ ] move core dataset and repo classes into `dataset/`(gather from `support/` and `distiribution/`)\n- [ ] in the spirit of #2765, introduce `core/` for a minimal set of commands that serve as the foundation for others and receive special scrutiny regard API composition and changes. Candidates are\n    - [ ] `status`\n    - [ ] `diff`\n    - [ ] `save`\n    - [ ] `create`\n    - [ ] `run`\n- [ ] `distributed/` -- key commands needed for communication with other dataset instances\n   - [ ]  `clone`\n   - [ ]  `install`\n   - [ ]  `get`\n   - [ ]  `update`\n   - [ ]  `publish`\n   - [ ]  `siblings`\n   - [ ]  possibly `drop`\n- [ ] `metadata/` -- this is largely already the case, but added from completeness\n  - [x] `metadata`\n  - [x]  `aggregate-metadata`\n  - [ ] `extract-metadata` (coming via -revolution)\n\nOther (more \"leafy\") commands could either be injected in these categories, or populate to additional ones, to possibly better indicate (and enforce?) their (in)dependence on/from others:\n- remove\n- uninstall\n- subdatasets\n- unlock\n- clean\n- ls\n- rerun\n- run-procedure\n- create-sibling*\n- export-*\n- search\n- add*\n- download-url","files":null}]}